V7 -- the two branches of p = P(a) and where they put the solar system and the dwarfs
    self-consistency a = -grad P/rho = -P'(a) grad a/rho: a = 0 (free fall, p = 0, CDM-like) or the supported branch a = g
    (static in the source's frame). A star orbits THROUGH the galaxy's medium at ~200 km/s, so no medium is static in its
    frame: the Sun carries NO phantom -> EFE quadrupole Q2 = 0, extra mass inside Saturn = 0, and wide binaries are
    Newtonian, gamma_v = 1.000 at every separation: inside the registered Arm-B ceilings (1.045/1.030), OUTSIDE the
    registered Arm-A band (1.16-1.23). The medium reading and the force-law reading are DR4-separable.
    [canonical] Draco-like dwarf (sigma 9 km/s, r_h 200 pc, L 3e5, d 76 kpc, v 200 km/s): M_dyn/L = 50; stripped of its medium it shows sigma = 1.8 km/s; host medium 9.1e-05 M_sun/pc^3: ram/support = 2.40
    [alt] Draco-like dwarf (sigma 9 km/s, r_h 200 pc, L 3e5, d 76 kpc, v 200 km/s): M_dyn/L = 50; stripped of its medium it shows sigma = 1.8 km/s; host medium 1.0e-04 M_sun/pc^3: ram/support = 2.63
  [PASS] V7 [THE PRESSURE-SUPPORTED DWARFS ARE THE NAMED KILL CONDITION] a dwarf keeps its dark dynamics only if its bound medium survives passage through the host's medium; the ram-pressure-to-support ratio is computed and compared with 1
           (ratio 2.40 / 2.63: order unity, MARGINAL -- neither a pass nor a kill; a stripped dwarf would show 1.8 km/s against 9 observed, so the stripping calculation decides)

